        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Tenochtitlan</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1325 CE – 1521 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">By the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> on a small island in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-texcoco">Lake Texcoco</a>; the exact date is unclear, and 13 March 1325 was chosen in 1925 for the 600th anniversary</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On an island in what was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-texcoco">Lake Texcoco</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valley-of-mexico">Valley of Mexico</a>, now the historic centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">Capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/templo-mayor">Templo Mayor</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinampa">chinampas</a>; causeways and canals; the market of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlatelolco">Tlatelolco</a>; the palace of Moctezuma; the fall of 1521</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Its ruins lie in the historic centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a>, which Cortés founded on the site.</span></div>
